{"files": [{"id": 69169930, "name": "sp6c00221_si_001.pdf", "size": 2247067, "is_link_only": false, "download_url": "https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/69169930", "supplied_md5": "7b17e5151f8202c300164a6f34f764e2", "computed_md5": "7b17e5151f8202c300164a6f34f764e2", "mimetype": "application/pdf"}], "folder_structure": {}, "authors": [{"id": 9765990, "full_name": "Hayley\nA. Bunn", "first_name": "Hayley\nA.", "last_name": "Bunn", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 25081105, "full_name": "Holdson H. Liang", "first_name": "Holdson H.", "last_name": "Liang", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1333506, "full_name": "Brian J. Esselman", "first_name": "Brian J.", "last_name": "Esselman", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1302183, "full_name": "Paul L. Raston", "first_name": "Paul L.", "last_name": "Raston", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 25081108, "full_name": "Andi Pracko", "first_name": "Andi", "last_name": "Pracko", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 25081111, "full_name": "Steven Shipman", "first_name": "Steven", "last_name": "Shipman", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 8562126, "full_name": "Brant Billinghurst", "first_name": "Brant", "last_name": "Billinghurst", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 1855051, "full_name": "Jianbao Zhao", "first_name": "Jianbao", "last_name": "Zhao", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 7021847, "full_name": "Jes K. J\u00f8rgensen", "first_name": "Jes K.", "last_name": "J\u00f8rgensen", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}, {"id": 8989322, "full_name": "Susanna L. Widicus Weaver", "first_name": "Susanna L.", "last_name": "Widicus Weaver", "is_active": false, "url_name": "_", "orcid_id": ""}], "custom_fields": [], "figshare_url": "https://acs.figshare.com/articles/journal_contribution/A_High-Resolution_Rotational_Analysis_of_2_Chloroethanol_HOCH_sub_2_sub_CH_sub_2_sub_Cl_and_Its_First_Vibrationally_Excited_State/33950716", "download_disabled": false, "description": "An extensive analysis of the high-resolution rotational\nspectrum\n(8\u201326 GHz, 140\u2013700 GHz, 100\u2013600 cm<sup>\u20131</sup>) of the simplest stable chlorohydrin, 2-chloroethanol, is provided\nby combining high-resolution infrared, microwave, and millimeter-wave\nspectra. The ground state and first vibrationally excited state of\nboth chlorine isotopologues (HOCH<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>2</sub><sup>35</sup>Cl and HOCH<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>2</sub><sup>37</sup>Cl) are well treated\nusing a single-state distorted rotor Hamiltonian in the A reduction\nand I<sup><i>r</i></sup> representation, reporting up to\na full set of octic distortion constants. The extended microwave spectrum\ncollected and the well-resolved quadrupole splitting observed therein\nallowed for the further refinement of quadrupole coupling parameters.\nInclusion of rotationally resolved infrared transitions enabled the\naccurate and precise determination of the vibrational band origin\nof \u03bd<sub>21</sub> for HOCH<sub>2</sub>CH<sub>2</sub><sup>35</sup>Cl (150.908 599 5 (43) cm<sup>\u20131</sup>). The high spectral\ndensity made measurement and least-squares fitting of transitions\nin both rotational and high-resolution infrared spectra challenging\nand is the likely source of the larger-than-expected \u03c3<sub>fit</sub> value of up to 0.060 MHz for each fit. Nevertheless, the extended\nmillimeter-wave spectrum reported here provides spectral frequencies\nthat directly overlap with astronomical data, allowing for a more\nthorough search for this species in the interstellar medium. Despite\nits expected formation from HCl with either oxirane or ethylene glycol\nin the interstellar medium, 2-chloroethanol continues to evade detection.\nWe report upper limits on the column density toward 30 astrophysically\ndiverse regions. The reported upper limits do not provide significant\nnew constraints on the chemistry of this species in the interstellar\nmedium and highlight the limited knowledge of interstellar chlorine\nchemistry.", "funding": null, "funding_list": [], "version": 1, "status": "public", "size": 2247067, "created_date": "2026-09-21T07:10:32Z", "modified_date": "2026-09-21T07:10:32Z", "is_public": true, "is_confidential": false, "is_metadata_record": false, "confidential_reason": "", "metadata_reason": "", "license": {"value": 10, "name": "CC BY-NC 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/"}, "tags": ["vibrational band origin", "simplest stable chlorohydrin", "reported upper limits", "report upper limits", "quadrupole coupling parameters", "provides spectral frequencies", "octic distortion constants", "908 599 5", "37 </ sup", "35 </ sup", "wave spectrum reported", "well treated using", "resolution rotational spectrum", "21 </ sub", "resolution rotational analysis", "2 \u2011 chloroethanol", "2 </ sub", "interstellar chlorine chemistry", "fit </ sub", "r </", "resolution infrared", "sup ><", "></ sup", "wave spectra", "extensive analysis", "chlorine isotopologues", "interstellar medium", "thorough search", "squares fitting", "precise determination", "limited knowledge", "likely source", "ground state", "full set", "expected \u03c3", "expected formation", "evade detection", "ethylene glycol", "either oxirane", "directly overlap", "chloroethanol continues", "astronomical data", "060 mhz"], "keywords": ["vibrational band origin", "simplest stable chlorohydrin", "reported upper limits", "report upper limits", "quadrupole coupling parameters", "provides spectral frequencies", "octic distortion constants", "908 599 5", "37 </ sup", "35 </ sup", "wave spectrum reported", "well treated using", "resolution rotational spectrum", "21 </ sub", "resolution rotational analysis", "2 \u2011 chloroethanol", "2 </ sub", "interstellar chlorine chemistry", "fit </ sub", "r </", "resolution infrared"